# Flutter Movie App — Project Standards

This is a **Clean Architecture, feature-first** TMDB movie app.

## Stack

- State: **Cubit only** (`flutter_bloc`) — no BLoC events by default
- i18n: `easy_localization` — `'key'.tr()` for all UI text; update `en.json` + `ar.json`
- Network: `DioClient` in `core/network/` — no raw `Dio()` in features
- Storage: Hive (cache), `flutter_secure_storage` (tokens), `shared_preferences` (flags)

## Layer Rules

- Features live under `lib/features/<name>/` with `data/`, `domain/`, `presentation/`
- Presentation → domain use cases/repositories (abstract), never data impls
- Data implements domain contracts; uses `core/` for Dio and storage
- Shared design tokens: `AppColors`, `AppSpacing`, `AppTypography` in `core/constants/`

## Before Implementing

Read `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/development-workflow.md`.

## Do Not

- Hardcode secrets (use `.env` + `AppConfig`)
- Hardcode user-facing strings or theme values in widgets
- Use `setState` for API-driven state
- Commit `.env`

## Commits

Conventional commits: `feat(movies):`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:` — only when user asks to commit.
